    "notes": "### Fixed\n\n- **The signal shows \"—\" when there is no reading, not Excellent.** Bluetooth's signal reading is dB from the ideal range, where 0 is ideal, and the Pico 2 W page's Signal graph showed a missing reading as 0, so right after connecting (or when a reading failed) it said 0 dB, Excellent. It now says \"—\" with no rating and leaves a gap in the graph. With firmware 0.9.5-dev.16 the board also tells the app when it has no reading; the OLED's BT Signal screen now uses the same dB scale and the same words as the app (Excellent / Good / Fair / Weak).",
